        "id": 101728,
        "name": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "username": "TheSoundOfTrees",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/da6949/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2014-05-10T10:54:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hello !</p><p>As I said on BGG, as long as you have fun playing, who cares if you followed exactly the rules or missed something :) Some of my most memorable games were full of mistakes - I remember a glorious fight against Aposate (all heroes down but Nightmist with 1 HP) that I won in an awesome way... until I understood that I had erronously redirected damage and should have been defeated. You know what ? I still count it as a victory, it was too awesome.</p><p>Baron Blade may be \"weak\" compared to other villains, and easy to defeat when you played often, but I still lose against him from time to time. And I like to tell the story of my first few games of Sentinels, and how I lost the first 5 or 6 to a maniacally laughing Baron. Most of the time with the Baron near full health.</p>",
